{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1787111854,"nonce":"0YTBgVpp72SWf6wZkQen6ayaahM=","message":"Decided and recorded in `8075ea2`, pushed to `main`.\n\n**The decision: the keys STAY, permanently inert** — own names, `orgs.settings`, bounds unchanged — on the standing rule ADR 0040 §6 applied to `refire_grace`: deleting or moving a settings key is a contract change of its own.\n\nRecorded in **ADR 0042 Amendment 3**, restated in **SPEC §B.3** beside the `refire_grace` ruling it follows. That is the \"one place\" this ticket asked for: the state it ends is exactly the one it named — four files each observing the keys decide nothing and none of them being the decision.\n\n**The amendment says where the two rulings DIFFER rather than reading as a copy of §6.** `refire_grace` is inert at its own layer but still PINS two numbers outside it (its floor at `2 x DedupTTL`, and `group_close_delay_s` at or above itself), each held by a named test. These three pin nothing at all, so the case for keeping them is genuinely weaker. What tipped it is that the operator-facing cost was already paid down by `235f347`: the row now states the retirement at every value, at level `inert`, with no `suggest`. A key that announces its own inertness is a much smaller tax than one that pretends to work.\n\n⭐ **The counter-argument is recorded, not defeated.** oto has no installs, so a settings-contract change is cheaper today than it will ever be again, and a key that pins nothing and does nothing is the clearest deletion candidate this schema has. The amendment lists exactly what moves together if that trade is taken — `AllSettingKeys`, the SettingKey constants, `settingBounds`, `SettingsPatch` + `intPtr`, the Settings fold, the DTOs and mapper, `orgs.settings` with a migration, `tuningCopy.ts`, the Helm values — **and that the declarative layer's boot refusal must be handled explicitly for a values file still naming a removed key, or the upgrade is a crash loop rather than a warning.**\n\nReopen and take that trade if you would rather spend the contract change now. The decision is written so it can be reversed deliberately instead of drifting.","files":null}]}